# Testing Rules

## General Testing Principles

### Test Coverage

- Aim for high test coverage (80%+ for critical paths)
- Test all public APIs and functions
- Test error scenarios and edge cases
- Test both success and failure paths
- Test integration points

### Test Organization

- Organize tests by feature/domain
- Use descriptive test names
- Group related tests together
- Use proper test fixtures
- Implement proper test setup and teardown

### Test Quality

- Write readable and maintainable tests
- Use proper assertions
- Test one thing per test
- Avoid test interdependencies
- Use proper mocking strategies

## Flutter/Dart Testing

### Unit Testing

- Test business logic in isolation
- Mock external dependencies
- Test all public methods
- Test error handling
- Use proper test data

### Widget Testing

- Test UI components
- Test user interactions
- Test widget state changes
- Test navigation flows
- Test responsive behavior

### Integration Testing

- Test complete user flows
- Test app startup
- Test authentication flows
- Test data persistence
- Test cross-platform behavior

### Test Structure

```dart
group('Feature Name', () {
  setUp(() {
    // Setup test data
  });

  tearDown(() {
    // Cleanup
  });

  test('should do something when condition', () {
    // Arrange
    // Act
    // Assert
  });
});
```

### Mocking

- Mock Firebase services
- Mock external APIs
- Mock file system operations
- Mock network requests
- Use proper mock verification

